Alright here it is.

I started as chaotic elven wizard with a magic marker (0:39) and a
potion of gainn level and gain ability. So nothing special. On dlvl 4
I found a sink and on dlvl 6 i found a co-aligned altar and the
entrance to Sokoban. After a quick dive to the mines i managed to get
my AC to -2. Then I decided to farm brown puddings for a source of
perma Elbereth. After 14k turns I got a wand of lightning. After that
I did the quest and then went back up to the sink, spawned a black
pudding and lured it down to dlvl 6 to set up a boulder fort and farm
for the required items for staying 2 billion turns in sokoban.

First I needed a ring of slow digestion so I could bridge the time for
the prayer timeout. Then I needed at least 20 cursed scrolls of
genocide to fill the whole sokoaban level with blue jellies as they
don't move and thus don't use up CPU time. To speed up the process
even more I hid all the messages with the MSGTYPE=hide option.
Furthermore I needed gauntlets of power to prevent my strength from
going down one point when going from hungry to weak. Also I removed
all unnecessary informations displayed in the status bar. (like turns,
score etc.)

After getting lucky and finding a WoW from a death drop I went down to
castle and got the other wand and therefore made my turn-overflow kit
complete.

So i packed all my stuff I needed for ascension into my boH, went to
Sokoban and filled the whole level with jellies. Then i removed all
rings and amulets and started my first paste.
send n99999.
After that my character gets hungry and after another paste of this
weak. (The character automatically stops waiting when something
happens e.g. status change or monster attacking). To fix the weak
status I prayed to Anhur which fixed it and then another round
started. One cycle was 17k turns so there was enough time to make sure
Anhur won't get angry. (I guess i even could've been crowned).
Unluckily I noticed NAO kept crashing after 300 cycles. (5.100.000
turns). So i decided to do 200 cycles (3.400.000 turns) and after that
save and resume. (NAO kept crashing nevertheless and several times I
lost several million turns)

I planned in 80k turns to ascend which was more than enough 'cause
through the above pudding farming I was more than ready to ascend.
After hitting the limit I said goodbye to my jellies and went on my
way to gehe. Nothing special about that. I just ran through the mazes
and didn't care for alchemy and stuff.
Then finally i arrived at the Astral plane. After a short chat with
Famine and the high priestess of Ptah I moved on to Death and to my
matching altar. Then I blocked the door to the temple with a wished up
boulder and filled all the Astral plane tiles with either ants or acid
blobs. Next thing to do was sit out more than 70k turns...

I only took like 6 or 7 K-Rations and a few lembas wafers with me...
big mistake as I noticed later. I had to wish up for a horn of plenty
and wrote some charging scrolls with my magic markers. And well ...
several turns later I hit maxint turns.

s, #offer, What do you want to sacrifice? u - the Amulet of Yendor
named real.......
and *poof* I ascended with -maxint turns.

